# Drive Precise — environment variables.
#
# Copy to .env.local for development. In production these are set in the Vercel
# project settings. Nothing here is secret: the publishable key is designed to
# be shipped to browsers, and every table it can reach is protected by RLS.
#
# The service role key is deliberately NOT listed. Nothing in this app needs it,
# and adding it to a Vite project would inline it into the client bundle.

# ── Supabase (required) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_xxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Same values, read during server-side rendering.
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_xxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ── Business details (optional overrides) ────────────────────────────────
#
# The real contact details ship as defaults in src/lib/business.ts, so a deploy
# that forgets these still shows the correct ones. Set them only to point a
# staging build somewhere else.
#
# VITE_BUSINESS_PHONE is the international form used by tel: links and
# structured data. VITE_BUSINESS_PHONE_DISPLAY is the national form people
# read. They must be the same number. VITE_WHATSAPP_NUMBER becomes a wa.me
# link, so it must be the number that actually has WhatsApp on it.
VITE_BUSINESS_PHONE=+447466338404
VITE_BUSINESS_PHONE_DISPLAY=07466 338404
VITE_WHATSAPP_NUMBER=+447466338404
VITE_BUSINESS_EMAIL=hello@driveprecise.co.uk
# Trade enquiries land in the same inbox. Do not point this at an address that
# has not been created: it receives the highest-value enquiries on the site.
VITE_BUSINESS_TRADE_EMAIL=hello@driveprecise.co.uk

# ── Company details (legally required for a UK Ltd company) ──────────────
#
# Both ship as defaults. They are mandatory disclosures under the Companies
# (Trading Disclosures) Regulations 2015 and the E-Commerce Regulations 2002,
# so they must not depend on an environment variable being remembered.
#
# The registered office is rendered only in the footer's legal line. It is not
# a place customers may turn up to (§55), so it never appears as a "visit us"
# address and never with a map.
VITE_COMPANY_NUMBER=15264715
VITE_REGISTERED_ADDRESS=26 Greenlands Road, Camberley, Surrey, GU15 2RT

# Drive Precise Ltd is NOT VAT registered. Leave this empty. Setting it while
# the company is unregistered is an offence, and the admin dashboard will flag
# the mismatch. If the company registers later, set this AND flip
# `vatRegistered` in src/lib/business.ts.
VITE_VAT_NUMBER=

# ── Vehicle lookup (UKVD primary, DVLA fallback) ─────────────────────────
#
# NOT set here. These are the only genuinely secret values in the project and
# must never appear in a VITE_ variable: Vite inlines those into the client
# bundle, publishing the key to every visitor.
#
# They belong in the Supabase edge function's secrets:
#
#   supabase secrets set UKVD_API_KEY=...
#   supabase secrets set UKVD_PACKAGES="VehicleData,VehicleImageData"
#   supabase secrets set LOOKUP_HASH_SALT="$(openssl rand -hex 16)"
#   supabase functions deploy vehicle-lookup
#
# UKVD_PACKAGES is a cost control, not a feature flag. Drive Precise is billed
# per package, so only the ones actually on the plan may be listed. Anything
# omitted degrades silently rather than erroring or, worse, being charged for.
# Recognised: VehicleData, MotHistory, VehicleImageData, TyreData, BatteryData,
# SpecAndOptionsData, ValuationData, VdiCheckFull.
#
# UKVD_BASE_URL overrides the API host if UKVD ever moves it.
#
# ── DVLA fallback (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Also a secret, also set through Supabase, never in a VITE_ variable:
#
#   supabase secrets set DVLA_API_KEY=...
#
# Free from https://developer-portal.driver-vehicle-licensing.api.gov.uk/,
# though they are not issuing new registrations at the time of writing, which
# is why UKVD is primary. Keeping DVLA configured is still worthwhile: if UKVD
# is unreachable or the account lapses, degrading to make and year is much
# better than degrading to nothing.
#
# With neither key set, the lookup returns "not_configured" and the quote form
# behaves exactly as it did before the feature existed: the customer types
# their own vehicle details. Nothing breaks and nothing is invented.

# ── TechMan GMS (§28) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# TechMan is where the business actually runs: the diary, estimates, invoices
# and payments. These two hostnames are the customer-facing half of it. Neither
# is secret — a customer's browser visits both — so VITE_ is correct here.
#
# VITE_TECHMAN_BOOKING_URL is the "web booking" site TechMan issued. It is the
# [URL] from TechMan's integration reference: /book loads `integrate.js` from
# it and embeds the booking flow. It must ALSO be listed in the CSP in
# vercel.json under script-src, frame-src and connect-src — csp.test.ts fails
# the build if the two disagree, because a mismatch renders a blank page with
# no visible error.
#
# Do NOT confuse this with TechMan's own "Web Booking URL" setting
# (Settings > Sites), which is this site's /book page, not the host below.
# Setting that field to the TechMan host makes every reminder link bypass the
# website entirely.
VITE_TECHMAN_BOOKING_URL=https://drivepreciseltd.wsptm.com

# The customer portal: where an estimate is read, authorised and paid. This is
# a native TechMan feature and needs no integration — the site only links to it
# so somebody sent an estimate last week has a way back. Unset means no link is
# rendered anywhere.
VITE_TECHMAN_PORTAL_URL=https://drivepreciseltd.portal.wsptm.com

# Deep-link parameters, UNSET until TechMan support confirm them.
#
# TechMan's Vehicle Reminder links preselect both a labour slot and a vehicle,
# so the parameters exist — but the names are not in the public documentation
# and are not worth guessing: a wrong parameter is silently ignored, so the
# link would look like it worked while losing the preselection it exists for.
# With these unset, "Book this now" still opens a working booking flow.
# VITE_TECHMAN_SLOT_PARAM=
# VITE_TECHMAN_REG_PARAM=

# ── Site ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used for canonical URLs and Open Graph tags. No trailing slash.
VITE_SITE_URL=https://www.driveprecise.co.uk

# ── Social (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_INSTAGRAM_URL=
VITE_FACEBOOK_URL=
